On Aug 28, 2:21=A0pm, rpresser <rpres...@gmail.com> wrote:
> But now I see that's not true, of course; only the record file is
> read back in and examined.
>
> The good news is that the record and logfiles seem to have
> exactly the same format, so it would still work the same.

Correct, only the record file is read back in. This is probably a good
thing for larger systems, as the logfile can get reasonably large.

On NAO,

zaphod:# wc record
  2000  32460 178114 record
zaphod:# wc logfile
  549443 10240246 49218101 logfile

You can see the logfile is 549000 lines to the 2000 record lines. It
weighs in at a hefty 49MB too. From a parsing perspective, the latter
file can be a bit cpu intensive for some operations. (At least if
performed on a regular basis.)

As always, both NAO files are available to the public, in case you
want to do any of your own analysis on larger files:

http://alt.org/nethack/record
http://alt.org/nethack/logfile

